Runtime software
----------------

The direct runtime Python dependencies are:

* FunASR 1.3.29 — MIT
* NumPy 2.4.6 — BSD-3-Clause AND 0BSD AND MIT AND Zlib AND CC0-1.0
* python-multipart 0.0.20 — Apache-2.0
* PyYAML 6.0.2 — MIT
* Starlette 0.47.2 — BSD-3-Clause
* PyTorch 2.11.0+cpu — BSD-3-Clause; its distribution also includes NOTICE
* TorchAudio 2.11.0+cpu — BSD-2-Clause
* Uvicorn 0.35.0 — BSD-3-Clause

The exact resolved package set is recorded in uv.lock. License and NOTICE files
shipped by the actual Python wheels are retained in their installed
distribution metadata under /opt/botified-asr. In the CPU container, license
materials for the Python base image and Debian packages, including ffmpeg and
ca-certificates, remain under /usr/share/doc and their respective installed
locations. Those upstream terms continue to apply.

